<title>RUSSIA: Yeltsin says Russia-Belarus currency union distant.</title>
<headline>Yeltsin says Russia-Belarus currency union distant.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A currency union between Russia and Belarus, which are signing a union treaty on Wednesday, is relatively far off, President Boris Yeltsin said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have a lot to do before introducing a single currency,&quot; Yeltsin said before the signing ceremony. He added the union would not create a single state. Both members would retain their sovereignty, and the union budget would be used to finance joint economic programmes.</p>
</text>
